ot their addresses"] [37 1 "// ImageModule compiles the module in file (unit's) into its image at out."] [65 1 "// ImageFresh reports whether out is the image of file as it is now."] [91 1 "// ---- the writer ----"] [99 1 "// strTab is an image's string table: the module's part and the code's share it."] [122 1 "// the literal values' tags"] [192 1 "// the nodes' tags"] [206 11 "// a tuple's worker as a constructor (unused)"] [336 1 "// encodeModule is the image of a module's forms."] [350 2 "// a loader of its own: names and constructors are records, nothing is loaded or run"] [447 2 "// the file: header, string table, module, code"] [462 1 "// closure writes a top-level closure's compiled code, or the error compiling it gives (raised when entered)."] [499 1 "// ---- the reader ----"] [711 1 "// imgSpan is a top-level closure's code in its module's image."] [714 1 "// loadImage loads a module from its image (as loadForms from its forms)."] [745 2 "// phase 0: the binders (strings, then bindings: their order in the image)"] [758 2 "// the bindings, read once: closures made at once, constructors' atoms after every binder is known"] [795 2 "// phase 1: the objects"] [822 2 "// phase 2: the constructors' fields"] [833 1 "// atom0 skips an atom (its literal's string literal not made)."] [850 1 "// reg registers a top-level binder of the module."] [860 1 "// compileImage decodes a top-level closure's code from its module's image."] [875 1 "// imgStrs is the image's string table (read again: the module keeps only the bytes)."] [890 1 "// imagePath is a module's image under the image directory, or \"\" when there is none or it is stale."] [899 1 "// SetImageDir makes the machine load the libraries' modules from their images in dir when they are fresh."] [902 1 "// Images is the number of modules loaded from their images."] [905 1 "// BuildImages writes the image of every module of the units in libs (as the loader finds them) that has no fresh"] [906 1 "// one under out, jobs at a time: the images made, those already fresh, the errors."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[55 49] [59 39] [77 32] [239 27] [339 20] [400 24] [468 21] [619 16] [666 16] [675 16] [728 17] [728 25] [731 18] [731 26] [752 17] [752 25] [790 14] [790 23] [939 12] [939 22]]} (go/file "image.go" :imports [


